					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1175130#post-4129811</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1175130/a-world-s-legacy#post-4129811</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 25 Jan 2019 00:21:41 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Monteparnas</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2926286</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I thought it bland and forced, a cliché for the sake of cliché.</p> <p>Why did the Foundation lied to her? Why did they waited 13 years to do it? Why didn't they prepared for a single moment for a possible escape if this was their very reason to not get them together in the first place years before? Why does she believe the Death Lizard all of a sudden? Why does the lizard get so warm toward someone it doesn't really know? How does the lizard achieves to escape with the added concern of not killing her, after being unable to (truly) escape for so many years? How does the Foundation fails so miserably to be laughable? How did 682 knew where to go to found other skips at all?</p> <p>The concept isn't bad, but it isn't actually new, either, and the execution just forces its way to the end without real development of anything. I suggest that the author try again with a lot of more work.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
